        <body>
            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0263" n="170" xml:id="pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/255: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-26T13:00:00-04:00">October 26, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>261. From Gibson. My 256, October 24, 4 p.m. After several weeks of delay due to
                    the systematic obstruction of the Peruvian delegate mediators last night agreed
                    upon text of declaration that war is at an end. This document will be
                    communicated to the parties at a plenary meeting on Monday. [Gibson.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
